{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1217042-best-place-to-learn-about-totems","id":1217042,"title":"Best place to learn about Totems?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-09T10:26:03-07:00","id":1217042,"title":"Best place to learn about Totems?","content":"M20 core's Totem background, and the Totems given in the Appendix, are pretty neat. I'm sure we'll get an expanded list of Totems and the Spirits that serve them in Gods, Monsters, Familiar Strangers, but I was wondering what book would be best to learn more about them in the meantime.<br /> <br /> The Man, Glitch and The Machine are all interesting options for technomages and technocrats of course. The animal totems are brilliant Shamanic entities, and that leaves a lot of room for variation.<br /> <br /> With that said, it occurred to me that there are many Traditions and Conventions who I couldn't really connect with a Totem. Now sometimes it just doesn't work. Hermetics who learn the Spirit sphere are not, in any sense, totemic or shamanic. Becoming the servant of a spirit is degrading and falls outside of common practice.<br /> <br /> But then you have the others. Sure, an Iterator could have The Machine, an Adept could have Glitch, and a NWO operative could have The Man. What kind of totem would find kinship with a Progenitor, representing a living alternative to Machine? A totem which embodies the biotechnological innovation of the Convention would be ideal. The same goes for an Etherite. Is there a totem which embodies raw energy and &quot;SCIENCE!!!&quot;? Is there a totem which embodies the infinite lust for material wealth which plagues the Syndicate? You get the idea.<br /> <br /> Furthermore it would be really great to read more about Glitch and The Machine, I find their writeups really fascinating. Are they described in Werewolf books, or previous editions of Mage?<br /> <br /> Also, can any powerful Spirit be a Totem Spirit? Or are Totem Spirits their own special class of Spirit? For example, could a greedy and destructive hypereconomist have The Wyrm (or one of its Incarna) as their Totem? Can spirits from the High Umbra be Totems? Or is it a Middle Umbra thing. I mean Coyote is a sort of &quot;animal spirit&quot;, but coyote spirits are below him in the hierarchy. They're definitely Middle Umbra. But the idea of Coyote, the Totem, is that within the High Umbra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-09-2018, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T11:10:01-07:00","id":1217055,"title":"","content":"Both Middle Umbral and High Umbral spirits can act as Totems. They seem to functionally work like Totems/avatars in Werewolf. Infinite Tapestry, Dreamspeakers and Spirit ways were the last book to talk about Totems. Infinite Tapestry has all the High Umbral Totem spirits.<br /> <br /> As for the right types of totem spirits and traditions I'll put an example up there.. Hermes is offered as a Totem in Infinite tapestry. While a Hermetic might now &quot;bow&quot; to a god patronage from a divine figure and attempting to become One with said entity might be on the table. For appropriate Etherite Totems, Adventurers have no problem finding the science in contacting advanced aliens..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T11:50:10-07:00","id":1217069,"title":"","content":"The only mages that would have the wyrm as a totem are the malfeans, one of the nephandi, and anyone who makes vocal their ties with the wyrm is literally asking for a werewolf to bite at their throat.<br /> <br /> As ever, Axis Mundi remains the go to guide for werewolf spirits. In there it explains how each totem embodies a particular ideologue. For example, Cockroach embodies the idea of survival and adaptation to one's environment. Unicorn embodies the idea of peace and protection, Gradnfather Thunder embodies sly cunning and quiet plotting, while Coyote embodies tricks.<br /> <br /> Someone from this forum actually made a pretty exhaustive list of werewolf totems from the various books. It's here: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/0By9UuUWWH6CiZTNGalFTdTNTdjA\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/f...TNGalFTdTNTdjA</a><br /> <br /> Dive in and have a look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T08:41:25-07:00","id":1217414,"title":"","content":"Thanks! That's all really useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}